cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both this release and the OSF preregistration that fixes the analysis plan."
title: "embryo-vc-bench: a preregistered, zero-wet-lab virtual-cell benchmark for early human embryo atlases"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-light evaluation harness testing whether zero-shot single-cell
  foundation models outperform naive baselines on surrogate in-silico
  perturbations built from public human preimplantation embryo atlases and on
  published out-of-domain CRISPRi differential-expression tables. The primary
  finding is a direction-magnitude dissociation: scale-free directional
  criteria improve while magnitude error is indistinguishable from the
  no-change baseline. The shared latent developmental time axis was never
  fitted; hypotheses H1 and H3 are reported as demoted or unexecutable.
authors:
